# The Irish Washerwoman (repertoire plan: irish-washerwoman). A new flatpicking arrangement of the
# 18th-century jig, in AABB form, in groups of three eighth notes (two groups to the bar).
# The guitar plays the tune at the written pitch of the fiddle part, which sounds an octave lower.
# A part: first position (finger 1 on fret 1, 2 on fret 2, 3 on fret 3).
# B part: fifth position for the high notes (finger 1 on fret 5, 3 on fret 7, 4 on fret 8). The
# repeated G-D pairs are fingers 4 and 3 (string 2 fret 8, string 3 fret 7); the F#-D pairs are
# both at fret 7 (strings 2 and 3), easiest with finger 3 laid flat across the two strings.
# Bar 7 of the B part stays in fifth position and uses the open B string; the open strings of its
# last bar give the hand time to move.
# Backup: G (320003), C (x32010), D (xx0232), down on each beat and up on the third eighth.
title: The Irish Washerwoman
